From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:16:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(backup): the .noopbak carries food, workouts and weekly
 reviews
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The backup held only the SQLite, settings.json and manifest.json, so a
restore onto a new phone brought back the strap history but an empty Food
tab, workouts without exercises and no weekly reviews.

VictorBackupFiles adds optional victor/* entries between settings.json and
manifest.json: files/food (log + thumbnails), files/training,
files/weekly, the fork's user prefs (goals, coach agenda switch, Mi día
view, automatic vibrations) and an end marker with the count. Never in the
copy: the Claude key and consent (encrypted store, never read), the
Tasker token and enable flag, the Google Tasks flag, the scale watermark.

Restore runs only after the new DB has landed and passed its check, is
all or nothing for our part (path whitelist, no .., size and count caps,
end marker), replaces only the folders the backup carries, and never fails
the DB restore. Older backups restore exactly as before.

Two hook lines in DataBackup (victor:backup); Settings blurb mentions
meals and that the Claude key is not in the copy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
